<zk xmlns:n="native">
	<label multiline="true">
		Steps to reproduce:
		1. Measure the prev/next arrow chevron against its own disc, over the light slide.

		- Expected: at least 3:1. The chevron is an essential graphical object, so
			SC 1.4.11 applies.
		- Bug: the disc backdrop was rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4), which composites to #999999
			over a light slide, leaving the white chevron at 2.85:1.

		2. Look at the arrow on the dark slide.

		- Expected: the disc still reads as a control. Contrast alone cannot do this
			(black on black at any alpha), so the arrow carries a light ring, the way
			zkmax scrollview's floating scrollbar does.
	</label>
	<carousel id="car" width="100%" height="220px">
		<carouselitem label="Light slide">
			<n:div id="lightSlide" style="height:100%;box-sizing:border-box;padding:50px 72px;background:#FFFFFF">
				<n:h2 style="margin:0;color:#1a4a73">Light slide</n:h2>
			</n:div>
		</carouselitem>
		<carouselitem label="Dark slide">
			<n:div id="darkSlide" style="height:100%;box-sizing:border-box;padding:50px 72px;background:#101418">
				<n:h2 style="margin:0;color:#dfe8f0">Dark slide</n:h2>
			</n:div>
		</carouselitem>
	</carousel>
</zk>
